  "published": "2025-12-23T12:48:33.67Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 2.0.5 brings significant simplification and performance improvements:\n\n**Authentication Simplification:**\n- SDK now uses ONLY API Key authentication (X-Api-Key header)\n- Removed all JWT/Bearer token authentication code\n- Simpler architecture with single authentication method\n- Cleaner and more maintainable codebase\n\n**Performance Improvements:**\n- Removed unnecessary authentication overhead\n- Every API call uses direct API Key authentication\n- No token management or caching complexity\n- Faster and more predictable behavior\n\n**Code Cleanup:**\n- Removed AuthenticateAsync() method (no longer needed)\n- Removed SetTokenWithJwtExpiry() method\n- Removed GetToken() method\n- Removed TokenResponse and TokenCache classes\n- Removed all JWT token handling code\n- Removed System.IdentityModel.Tokens.Jwt dependency\n- Removed System.Runtime.Caching dependency (no longer needed)\n- Removed all caching logic (not needed for API Key authentication)\n- Simplified AddStandardHeaders to use only API Key\n\n**New Features (from 2.0.4):**\n- Certificate: Digital certificate signature (ICP-Brasil compliant)\n- CloudCertificate: Cloud-based digital certificate\n- SelfieDoubleAuthentication: Selfie-based 2FA\n\n**Breaking Changes:**\n- AuthenticateAsync() method removed - if your code calls this method, simply remove those calls\n- SetTokenWithJwtExpiry() method removed - use API Key authentication instead\n- JWT token support completely removed\n\n**Migration:**\n- If you're using only SetCredential(new ApiKeyCredential(...)), no changes needed\n- If you're calling AuthenticateAsync(), simply remove those calls\n- All operations now work directly with API Key\n\nFor full documentation, visit: https://github.com/forsign/sdk-dotnet",
  "repository": "",
